        "title": "Open after the quake - worth a visit",
        "text": "Pashupatinath temple complex is sizable, and it is one of the Kathmandu UNESCO World Heritage sites to survive the April quakes with minimal damage. Non-hindus are not permitted to enter the main temple, but you can get good views of it from high on the other bank, and you can see plenty to other interesting sights including cremations. Pick up a local guide on the way in for an informative tour, and have your picture taken with the sahus (tips expected for both guide and sadhus).",
