        "title": "A must to go",
        "text": "I visited again Pashupatinath temple this year with my crew. It´s a wonderfull place where you can find peace and learn the history of Lord Shiva, one of majos deities for Hindus. All this temple is dedicated to Lord Shiva, also known as Pashupati. Sometimes can be a bit smelly because they cremated dead body all the time, but you can assist to ceremony from other side of river in a high place, away from the funeral. Don´t miss the pujas in the temple in end of day, with thousands of candles. Also you can see the big gold bull from outside of temple, they don´t allow non-Hindus inside the temple. ",
