      {
        "review_id": 275922037,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r275922037-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Lord Shiva's Temple",
        "text": "Pashupatinath is a must-visit temple for me every time I travel to Nepal. For Hindus, it is as important as the Dwadash-jyotirlingas or the 12 key Shiva temples which are located in India. A unique aspect of the deity is its four faces , one in each direction. During my recent visit, I went to the temple around 11 am on a Friday morning. I was pleasantly surprised that the ubiquitous queues were missing this time. I was able to spend ample time in front of each of the faces of the Lord without being pushed away by the priests as happens on the busy days. After the darshan, I spent time looking up some of the other temples in the complex. There are statues of some the Nepalese kings who had been involved in several constructions within the temple precinct. I watched with interest as many locals were offering prayers to a large idol of  Hanuman. I also explored a small temple established here by Adi Sankaracharya, the greatest exponent of Advaita philosophy. It was quite humbling to have visited this temple which has such a rich history.",
