      {
        "review_id": 271698588,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r271698588-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Great UNESCO heritage site , visit is a must !",
        "text": "Visited the Pashupatinath Temple complex on the afternoon of 1st January 2015 ,arranged by our guide , Mr Prasant from Outshine Adventures.\nThis temple is one of the most sacred Hindu temples of Nepal,dedicated to God Shiva.\nThe complex is located on both banks of Bagmati River on the east of Kathmandu city.\nThe main temple of Pashupatinath is a building with a bunk roof and a golden spire, on the west bank of Bagmati River ,considered as a masterpiece of Hindu architecture.\nAlong the right bank of Bagmati numerous platforms for funeral pyres are built. The cremations on these platforms are a common activity , and we witnessed some cremation process while we were there, the first open cremation we ever witnessed.\nThere's some chairs on the hills opposite the cremation area, facing towards Bagmati river.\nWe took photos with the Sadhus on little stupas opposite Bagmati river , of course with a small sum of money, be careful ,deal with them first before you take pictures.\nOverall , a one of a kind experience ,worth the time spent , we highly recommend a visit to all tourists visiting Kathmandu.\nWe hoped that no significant damage to the temple and surrounding building after the 25 April earthquake and the 12 May 2015 aftershock.",
